Knowledge Manager Demo
Standalone Application
14 Jun 2026

* Start the Knowledge Manager

Click Run to start the Knowledge Manager documentation server.

Run every command from the `applications/knowledge-manager-demo` root. The
catalog owns the canonical profile and UI; agent-core owns the development
runtime:

	export AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT="${AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT:-$(cd ../catalog && pwd)}"
	export AGENT_CORE_ROOT="${AGENT_CORE_ROOT:-$(cd ../../agent-core && pwd)}"

Open the running servers after they start:

- Documentation: [[http://localhost:18081][http://localhost:18081]]
- Control (lifecycle exit): [[http://127.0.0.1:18082][http://127.0.0.1:18082]]
- Monitor: [[http://localhost:18084/ui/][http://localhost:18084/ui/]]

Run the canonical catalog profile through an agent built from the selected
agent-core checkout:

	agent --profile "$AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT/agents/knowledge-manager/documentation-curator/profile.yaml" --directory "$AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT" --core-root "$AGENT_CORE_ROOT"

An installed runtime already owns `/opt/agent-core`; omit `--core-root`:

	agent --profile "$AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT/agents/knowledge-manager/documentation-curator/profile.yaml" --directory "$AGENT_CATALOG_ROOT"

* Call the lifecycle exit API

After the Knowledge Manager is running, post the exit request to its control
server (default `http://127.0.0.1:18082/api/lifecycle/exit`, HTTP 202 Accepted).
The request is itself a declarative agent, not a bespoke HTTP client: a four-state
machine moves from `Idle` to `Posting`, binds the REST operation, and then reaches
terminal `Done` or `Failed`. Run it through the same source-checkout interpreter:

	agent --profile "$(pwd)/call-lifecycle-exit/profile.yaml" --directory "$(pwd)" --core-root "$AGENT_CORE_ROOT"

With an installed runtime, omit `--core-root`:

	agent --profile "$(pwd)/call-lifecycle-exit/profile.yaml" --directory "$(pwd)"

The REST authority lives in the profile, not in runtime input:

.code call-lifecycle-exit/rest.yaml /post_exit:/,/signal: ExitAccepted/
